{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1548047-attribute-boost-limit","id":1548047,"title":"Attribute boost limit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-30T01:42:23-08:00","id":1548047,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Attribute boost limit","content":"Hello there!<br /> <br /> Asking for personal opinions here rather than interpretations of the manual RAW (a question for that was already asked elsewhere).<br /> <br /> This is referring to the 2nd edition of MtC and other splats.<br /> <br /> I don't see anything specifying that Attributes may be boosted only up to 10 through Pillar points.<br /> <br /> Do you think such a limit should be imposed for mechanical balance (also considering other splats), or is it fine to let an Arisen go up to Strength 35 for a scene and just roll with it, knowing that recovering Pillar points is a slow process?<br /> <br /> What would such attributes even look like if you're not rolling to determine outcome? What can Strength 35 achieve, for example? Or Intelligence? At such numbers I'd be inclined to inspire players with notions that <i>seem</i> beyond what could be deduced from the evidence available, but they'd be tapping into things like the cosmic mind or their genetic memory - stuff that's talked about in real world psychology and religions and which is not really farfetched in the world of CoD and MtC.<br /> <br /> Thanks to all participants in this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T03:55:49-08:00","id":1548137,"title":"","content":"On page 122, Using pillar section, the core says that you can boost Physical attributes once per scene by your Sekhem boosting score, so the &quot;worst case scenario&quot; would be a Strenght 10 mummy boosting to 14 (i would allow that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T06:07:56-08:00","id":1548140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1548047-attribute-boost-limit?p=1548137#post1548137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 122, Using pillar section, the core says that you can boost Physical attributes once per scene by your Sekhem boosting score, so the &quot;worst case scenario&quot; would be a Strenght 10 mummy boosting to 14 (i would allow that)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, unless I'm missing something. The following is based on the page you quoted plus page 123 plus the section on Sekhem and its table:<br /> <br /> Each Pillar point spent to raise Physical Attributes raises them by a number of dots determined by one's Sekhem. At Sekhem 10, for example, that number is 4, based on the Sekhem table. <br /> <br /> The number of Pillar points one can spend per turn is also based on Sekhem, but it's a different value. At Sekhem 10, that's 5 points per turn, based on the Sekhem table.<br /> <br /> So any mummy at Sekhem 10 can raise one of her Physical Attributes by 4 dots multiplied by 5 Pillar points for a scene, provided that they spend all the Pillar points in the same turn. That's +20 dots.<br /> <br /> A mummy can also spend points from her Defining Pillar to raise one of her Favored Attributes (the text could also be interpreted to mean both Decree's Favored Attributes at once) by one per point spent, once per scene.<br /> <br /> So a mummy with a Physical Attribute as Favored can give it +20 on the first turn of a scene and +5 on the second turn. The boost will last until the end of the scene. Any character who bought at least one extra Pillar dot at creation and has 5 dots in their Defining Pillar can do this, so it's viable from the start.<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, there are two Affinities that allow one to boost Mental and Social Attributes in the same way as Physical ones.<br /> <br /> So any mummy can have +25 in an Attribute in 2 turns, or +20 in one turn if it's not a Favored Attribute. If the Attribute is already at 10 dots, that makes it 35.<br /> <br /> And without complex gimmicks, with those two Affinities and without caring for which Attributes are Favored and which Pillar is Defining, any mummy can boost any Attribute by +20 for 5 unspecified Pillar points for a scene at Sekhem 10 (but only one Attribute per scene). Of course, that number goes down gradually with the Sekhem rating, but it's still significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T12:44:22-08:00","id":1548198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1548047-attribute-boost-limit?p=1548140#post1548140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly, unless I'm missing something. The following is based on the page you quoted plus page 123 plus the section on Sekhem and its table:<br /> <br /> Each Pillar point spent to raise Physical Attributes raises them by a number of dots determined by one's Sekhem. At Sekhem 10, for example, that number is 4, based on the Sekhem table.<br /> <br /> The number of Pillar points one can spend per turn is also based on Sekhem, but it's a different value. At Sekhem 10, that's 5 points per turn, based on the Sekhem table.<br /> <br /> So any mummy at Sekhem 10 can raise one of her Physical Attributes by 4 dots multiplied by 5 Pillar points for a scene, provided that they spend all the Pillar points in the same turn. That's +20 dots.<br /> <br /> A mummy can also spend points from her Defining Pillar to raise one of her Favored Attributes (the text could also be interpreted to mean both Decree's Favored Attributes at once) by one per point spent, once per scene.<br /> <br /> So a mummy with a Physical Attribute as Favored can give it +20 on the first turn of a scene and +5 on the second turn. The boost will last until the end of the scene. Any character who bought at least one extra Pillar dot at creation and has 5 dots in their Defining Pillar can do this, so it's viable from the start.<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, there are two Affinities that allow one to boost Mental and Social Attributes in the same way as Physical ones.<br /> <br /> So any mummy can have +25 in an Attribute in 2 turns, or +20 in one turn if it's not a Favored Attribute. If the Attribute is already at 10 dots, that makes it 35.<br /> <br /> And without complex gimmicks, with those two Affinities and without caring for which Attributes are Favored and which Pillar is Defining, any mummy can boost any Attribute by +20 for 5 unspecified Pillar points for a scene at Sekhem 10 (but only one Attribute per scene). Of course, that number goes down gradually with the Sekhem rating, but it's still significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ve still doubts about the exact rules, but considering the 1ed rules and a matter of balance my take on this is the following:<br /> <br /> Page 122 says you can use pillar points (plural) to boost physical attributes, but only once per scene.<br /> it also says that you can boost a Favored attribute (i forgot about those) by one dot per point spent, but again only once per scene.<br /> <br /> For a Sekhem 10 mummy i think that it means:<br /> Turn 1<br /> Spend 3 pillars to boost all 3 physical attributes by 4<br /> Turn 2<br /> Spend 5 points (per turn limit) to boost a favored physical attribute (if you have one)<br /> <br /> And then no more, but the boost persist for the whole scene, for an hypotetical maximum of +9 in one physical (pretty good indeed)<br /> <br /> I don t know if any of the Devs have clarified those rules, i haven t found any thread about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T13:45:23-08:00","id":1548203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1548047-attribute-boost-limit?p=1548198#post1548198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ve still doubts about the exact rules, but considering the 1ed rules and a matter of balance my take on this is the following:<br /> <br /> Page 122 says you can use pillar points (plural) to boost physical attributes, but only once per scene.<br /> it also says that you can boost a Favored attribute (i forgot about those) by one dot per point spent, but again only once per scene.<br /> <br /> For a Sekhem 10 mummy i think that it means:<br /> Turn 1<br /> Spend 3 pillars to boost all 3 physical attributes by 4<br /> Turn 2<br /> Spend 5 points (per turn limit) to boost a favored physical attribute (if you have one)<br /> <br /> And then no more, but the boost persist for the whole scene, for an hypotetical maximum of +9 in one physical (pretty good indeed)<br /> <br /> I don t know if any of the Devs have clarified those rules, i haven t found any thread about it</div> </div> </div> </div>The text on p.122 (or 123, I'm a bit tired now to check) says you can spend Pillar points (plural indeed) to raise <i>a single</i> Physical Attribute for a scene, once per scene. Otherwise your take would be fine.<br /> <br /> I have been mulling this over though, and I had a player who did it in session, and I realise it's not as much of a problem. Worst case scenario (Attribute at 10 + 35, Skill or other rolled Trait at 10) you roll 45 dice. Maybe more with Equipment and the Pillar bonus to some Skill rolls. But let's say 45: you average 15 successes and for one scene can tear through most enemies with one blow and destroy any physical object within reach - or solve riddles or sway the crowd, depending on the Attribute. That's fine. It's gonna take a while to recover 10 Pillar points, it's not gonna be too effective against the main Mummy antagonists, like other Mummies because they can also raise their Attributes to match yours - think of 40 dots in Health -, and it's not too hard to throw something else at the players to keep them on their toes. At the same time, spending 5 or 10 Pillars at once is not little, so you as ST don't need to have the NPCs do it frequently just because it can be done.<br /> <br /> In short: I think it works and translates well mechanically why mummies are such a menace in the world, able to keep even other supernaturals in check (imagine turning to ash a few vampire elders a few hours after waking up because they have offended you, and most supernaturals in the world don't know how often you can pull off something like this) and recruit them in their cults, and how they can replenish their cults' ranks so fast during a Descent. A well timed boost to Intelligence or Presence might be all that is needed to start one's Descent with the right foot, a genius plan incomprehensible to mortals and/or a massive following.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T15:35:00-08:00","id":1548207,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Once per scene&quot; part indicates to me that the rules are clumsily written. The most literal interpretation is that you can spend any number of Pillar points (within your Sekhem rating limits) and still only get a single Attribute boost for a single Attribute. This is weird and counterproductive, so I'm more inclined to believe that writing &quot;Pillar points&quot; in plural is a mistake, and that the intent is that you can only boost physical Attributes once in this way (though I'm very uncertain about whether you're supposed to be able to do it once per Attribute or once total per scene; the language implies the latter but the former makes more sense to me).<br /> <br /> Either way, that mummy might be mighty surprised if the elder vampire responds by rolling 65 dice for their counterattack (maxed Attribute &amp; Skill, maxed physical Discipline, maxed Physical Intensity, Frenzy bonuses). Though only for a maximum of five turns before they roll a measly 35 dice until their Frenzy goal is met.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T22:52:44-08:00","id":1548214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1548047-attribute-boost-limit?p=1548207#post1548207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Once per scene&quot; part indicates to me that the rules are clumsily written. The most literal interpretation is that you can spend any number of Pillar points (within your Sekhem rating limits) and still only get a single Attribute boost for a single Attribute. This is weird and counterproductive, so I'm more inclined to believe that writing &quot;Pillar points&quot; in plural is a mistake, and that the intent is that you can only boost physical Attributes once in this way (though I'm very uncertain about whether you're supposed to be able to do it once per Attribute or once total per scene; the language implies the latter but the former makes more sense to me).<br /> <br /> Either way, that mummy might be mighty surprised if the elder vampire responds by rolling 65 dice for their counterattack (maxed Attribute &amp; Skill, maxed physical Discipline, maxed Physical Intensity, Frenzy bonuses). Though only for a maximum of five turns before they roll a measly 35 dice until their Frenzy goal is met.</div> </div> </div> </div>But physical disciplines max out at 5 like the other disciplines in VtR 2e. So at max stats we're talking about 25 dice. 30 if we spend 1 Vitae to add a weapon bonus through Vigor. If we also spend 14 Vitae (the max is 15 per turn, but we spent 1 on Vigor) for Physical Intensity, we can add 28, going to 58. If Frenzying, we add 10, so 68. Ok you're right. Sorry, I had to do the maths and check the manual to jog my memory.<br /> <br /> That is terrifying indeed and would make for a hell of a fight.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T00:53:46-08:00","id":1548215,"title":"","content":"The active Vigor (or Praestantia for Dexterity-based attacks) effect adds damage, not dice, so I didn't count it. Assuming that the attack hits, each increased damage would correspond to three dice.<br /> Removing 2 dice from Physical Intensity, that's effectively 78 dice for five turns. Skipping Physical Intensity entirely and only adding the active Vigor &quot;dice&quot;, they can keep attacking with effectively 50 dice for 75 turns (assuming they don't feed at all, which they could as part of an attack during Frenzy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T01:11:18-08:00","id":1548216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1548047-attribute-boost-limit?p=1548215#post1548215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The active Vigor (or Praestantia for Dexterity-based attacks) effect adds damage, not dice, so I didn't count it. Assuming that the attack hits, each increased damage would correspond to three dice.<br /> Removing 2 dice from Physical Intensity, that's effectively 78 dice for five turns. Skipping Physical Intensity entirely and only adding the active Vigor &quot;dice&quot;, they can keep attacking with effectively 50 dice for 75 turns (assuming they don't feed at all, which they could as part of an attack during Frenzy).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really good. On the one side, it completely answers my question for the thread: it clearly isn't that much of an issue for a mummy at its peak power to raise an Attribute to 35. On the other side, it helps me take better stock of the capabilities of other supernaturals, which I hadn't pondered much at high levels, not playing those splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}